From 4cc768cc7e29cf1955b357760ac2e6fff63b0b0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Lane A <lane-a@local.invalid>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 11:25:22 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 01/18] feat(assets): licence-gated music/SFX variant library
 and keyless B-roll

- media/asset_library.py: a mood or SFX cue may have a variant folder
  (assets/<kind>/library/<name>/); the renderer picks one per clip from a
  stable hash of the clip id (re-renders keep their pick), never swaps an
  explicit track pick or a beat-grid clip's track. A profile's
  audio.sfx_pack draws from library/<pack>/<cue> first; meme_comedy uses
  the new synthesised "meme" pack. ASSET_VARIANTS=off restores stem files.
- assets/ASSET_MANIFEST.json + tools/assets/check_licences.py: every
  shipped audio file needs a manifest entry with matching sha256, a source
  and a licence in {CC0-1.0, PDM-1.0, original}; the gate prints
  "ship-clean" or blocks (391 files clean).
- tools/assets/fetch_library.py (Openverse CC0/PDM, Kenney CC0, FreePD
  checked against the archived freepd.com pages + archive MD5),
  curate_library.py (silence trim, loudness match, manifest),
  make_meme_sfx.py (original booms, boing, rimshot, sad trombone, ...),
  library_bundle.py (pack / verified install of the extended library,
  which stays out of git and out of the installer path per Sanji Q14).
- media/openverse_broll.py: third, keyless B-roll source (CC0/PDM photos
  as Ken Burns clips) behind the same relevance gate and vision veto;
  BROLL_OPENVERSE=off. Unit tests run with it off (autouse fixture).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
