@@ -5,6 +5,9 @@ What changed in SnipNova for people using the product. Newest dates are first.
 Add a line here when a pull request changes something a user can see. Use **New**, **Improved**, **Fixed**, or **Under the hood**, describe the change in plain language, and link the pull request. Skip internal-only work, or fold it into one **Under the hood** line. Do not include customer names, email addresses, user IDs, or anything else private.
 
 ## 2026-11-18
+- **New:** Auto clips no longer all sound the same once the extended library is installed (one command, checked file by file). Each music mood then has a library of free tracks, and each sound-effect cue has many variants. Every clip gets its own pick, and keeps it when it is re-rendered. New moods are available too: epic, suspense, emotional, cinematic and world. Everything shipped is public domain (CC0) or our own original, and the packaging check refuses any file without a recorded licence. Set `ASSET_VARIANTS=off` for the old one-file-per-mood behaviour. ([#TBD](https://github.com/FujiwaraChoki/supoclip/pulls))
+- **New:** Meme & comedy clips use a meme sound pack of our own: deep booms, boing, rimshot, sad trombone, slide whistle and more. ([#TBD](https://github.com/FujiwaraChoki/supoclip/pulls))
+- **New:** B-roll works without any stock API key. When Pixabay and Coverr are not set up, or find nothing, Auto clips use public-domain photos from Openverse as slow-zoom cutaways. They pass the same relevance checks. Set `BROLL_OPENVERSE=off` to turn this off. ([#TBD](https://github.com/FujiwaraChoki/supoclip/pulls))
 - **Improved:** The app background is now a dim Galaxy starfield — twinkling stars drifting slowly outward, parting subtly around the cursor — replacing the aurora bands. It stays dark and quiet behind everything, pauses when the tab is hidden, and holds still under reduced-motion settings. ([#TBD](https://github.com/FujiwaraChoki/supoclip/pulls))
 - **New:** Gaming streamer clips can now use the "Face on top, game below" layout from the create page — the facecam stacked over the gameplay with a red or gold divider, big words on the seam and an optional "credit @creator" line. The picker appears under Campaign & style when the niche is Gaming, and applies when framing is Auto (Fit and Crop keep their own layouts). ([#TBD](https://github.com/FujiwaraChoki/supoclip/pulls))
 - **Improved:** A clip now keeps one look from start to finish. Before, the picture could jump between a zoomed-in face crop and the whole frame with blurred bars every second or two. The app now picks whichever look covers most of the clip and uses it throughout. Two-person podcast splits and streamer facecam layouts are unchanged. Set `REFRAME_CONSISTENT=0` for the old shot-by-shot behaviour. ([#TBD](https://github.com/FujiwaraChoki/supoclip/pulls))
